    "longBusinessSummary": "DeNA Co., Ltd. develops and operates various mobile and online services in Japan and internationally. It operates DeNA games, a free-to-play mobile apps and browser games; Mobage, an entertainment platform; Yahoo! Mobage, which offers social games for PC browsers; AndApp, a platform that allows users to play mobile game apps on PC browsers under the same user account; Pococha, a social live streaming community; and IRIAM, an app where users can live stream as an anime characters. The company also operates kencom, which supports health insurance societies to manage their members' health data; and ONSEI, an AI-driven cognitive self-check app. In addition, it operates MENKYO, which enables cognitive function test for elderly drivers seeking license renewal; MOGI, a cognitive function test similar to MENKYO; SHINRI-ADAS, a cognitive functional test; Join, a communication app; MySOS, a life-saving and health support app with health and medical record for the user and their family; Team, a solution that connects medical and healthcare services and supports multi-professional collaboration; Join Mobile Clinic, an integrated telemedicine support solution that combines portable medical devices and Join; and Tsunaken, a health checkup online digital transformation solution. Further, the company operates DENA SPORTS GROUP, Yokohama DeNA Baystars, Kawasaki Brave Thunders, S.C.SAGAMIHARA, Virtual KEIBI System, DeNA AI, Strategic Investment Office, and Delight Ventures. DeNA Co., Ltd. was incorporated in 1999 and is headquartered in Shibuya, Japan.",
